  "lore": {
    "A": {
      "title": "Foot of the Sky-Stair",
      "text": "The sky-stair lands here, broken at the bottom as well. They built it to climb, and then they ran out of reasons. The last step is polished by feet."
    },
    "Y": {
      "title": "The Hall Where They Agreed",
      "text": "The two ages met in this hall, high-tech lords on one side and cultivators on the other. It took years. They called it the Accord."
    },
    "R": {
      "title": "Breath Under the Heart",
      "text": "The old stone says only this: the breath that lifts you is the breath that sets you down. Learn both and you do not fall.",
      "teaches": "cloudruins_art_3"
    },
    "G": {
      "title": "Why Balance",
      "text": "Written plain on the wall: if one side wins, the other side is gone, and then the winner starves. The Accord was not mercy. It was arithmetic."
    },
    "M": {
      "title": "The Forgetting",
      "text": "After the Accord, the people agreed to forget. Not the war, the hate. The rest slipped out with it. That is why you do not know your own history."
    },
    "O": {
      "title": "Five and the Cycle",
      "text": "Five of them, always. Each feeds the next and holds another in check. Take one out and the cycle limps. Put it back and it walks."
    },
    "U": {
      "title": "What the Survivor Left Out",
      "text": "Scratched low, by a tired hand: I told Eliet the Deep killed eight. It did not. We came wanting the Heart, out of balance, and the Deep set us right. Eight stayed, and I walked back alone."
    },
    "X": {
      "title": "Note to Whoever Comes Next",
      "text": "The Heart does not want your death. It wants you level. Put down what you carried too long, pick up what you left behind, and go home."
    }
  },
  "riddles": {
